# Default deny: a file is tracked only if a line below names it.
#
# The rule is one sentence: **tracked iff the build, the tests or the published package need
# it.** Prose, rounds of documents, experiment harnesses and their results stay on disk and in
# history, not in the tree.  git will not remind you -- .github/workflows/ci.yml runs
# `git status --porcelain` and fails on anything that is neither committed nor ignored.
#
# Every allowlist line is anchored with a leading slash: an unanchored `!README.md` would also
# un-ignore `docs/rounds/README.md`.
*
!*/

/.gitattributes
/.gitignore
/.editorconfig
/rustfmt.toml

/.cargo/
/.github/

/Cargo.toml
/Cargo.lock

/src/
/tests/

# The package front page and its licence, plus the documents code or tests read.
/LICENSE
/README.md
/CHANGELOG.md
/CONTRIBUTING.md
/SELF.mf
/docs/PROTOCOL.md
/docs/REPO.mf

# What the allowlist above would otherwise let through.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
target/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
